<Text>&lt;DIV style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-element: para-border-div; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; TEXT-ALIGN: center; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 1.0pt 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Single Channel&amp;nbsp;RF Impairment Modeling for&amp;nbsp;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; TEXT-ALIGN: center; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .75pt; mso-padding-alt: 0in 0in 1.0pt 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;Radar System Simulation &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;Simulation Task&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;This workspace demonstrates the 3-layer architecture based radar simulation with single channel Tx &amp;amp; Rx RF impairment modeling, using both the dataflow behavior RF models and Spectrasys RF models.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Workspace Description&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;This workspace is designed as a template to show the way to set up the arbitrary type radar simulation based on the generalized 3-layer framework and how to generate the echoes from the scatters of targets, together with RF impairment modeling capabilities. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&quot;&gt;The example includes three layers: trajectory layer, antenna layer&amp;nbsp;and signal layer. For waveform and signal processing design, we just give LFM and traditional pulse-compression and pulse-doppler results.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;This RF modeling capability is demonstrated by two ways, one is the behavioral models (mixers, amplifiers, filters) from the algorithm library (Design0 schematic), and the other is using the frequency domain models in the Spectrasys RF Design library and the channel is represented by RF_Link in the high-level simulation&amp;nbsp;(Design1 schematic).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;1) Behavioral RF Modeling (No additional license)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;This is the basic way to model the RF impairments for any radar system. This method is very straight-forward with very fast simulation speed, and only requires several basic parts to model a single RF channel (mixer -&amp;gt; amplifier -&amp;gt; BP filter, etc.), for instance. Also some fundamental RF modeling parameters are provided in each part for user input.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;2) Spectrasys RF_Link Modeling (Requires Spectrasys license)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;This is a more advanced way to model the RF impairments for any radar system. This method requires separate channel building for Tx &amp;amp; RF channels (see RF_Designs folder for more details), and user would need to establish RF Spectrasys analysis to analyze the RF impairments for both channels.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Although it seems complicated, the Spectrasys provides&amp;nbsp;more accurate frequency domain&amp;nbsp;analysis to the RF channels (frequency domain RFuW modeling methodology with Keysight IP), then transforms the freq-domain results back to dataflow. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;To create your own system, you can modify the template by changing parameters or replace models that are either in the radar/beamforming library or import your customized RF models in the design.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;I&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;NOTE: Spectrasys Filtering Delay Compensation Realized in the Design1 Schematic&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/I&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 13.5pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;One important point in Spectrasys RF_link modeling is the additional delayed sample issue caused by Spectrasys filters. User can read the Spectrasys filtering either from the additional automatic folders (in this case they are the Design1/2_Data_Folder) or the simulation log from the 1&lt;SUP&gt;st&lt;/SUP&gt; time simulation. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; COLOR: black; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-font-kerning: 12.0pt&apos;&gt;Then, for the 2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; time simulation, the compensation can be done using the Const + ChopVarOffset models after the pulse compression part. Related sample point calculation is simple and is presented in the Equation tab of Design1 schematic.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;&apos;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;The &#x201C;NoDelay&#x201D; dataset is generated by shorting (bypassing) all filters in Tx &amp;amp; RF spectrasys RF designs, and the &#x201C;TxRxFltrDelay&#x201D; dataset is generated by enabling all the filters (except the 1st BPF in Tx channel)&amp;nbsp;in both designs. It can be observed that by compensating these delays, the pulse compression Range-Doppler spectrum maps and PD results are identical.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
